  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case12",
  "description": "WS-TRANID-SUFFIX counts from 000001 upwards and IS NEVER RESET, not even at an account break. Four records across three accounts produce identifiers 2022071800000001 through 2022071800000004 in that exact order: ADD 1 TO WS-TRANID-SUFFIX at :474 runs once per write and nothing anywhere in the program moves zero back into it, so the counter is a property of the RUN rather than of the account. The identifier is the concatenation the STRING at :476-480 builds - PARM-DATE PIC X(10) followed by WS-TRANID-SUFFIX PIC 9(06), which is exactly the sixteen bytes of TRAN-ID PIC X(16) - so the suffix is zero-filled to six digits and the boundary between the two operands is fixed. Two breaks happen along the way, rewriting accounts 1 (194.00 + 12.50 + 25.00 = 231.50) and 2 (158.00 + 12.50 = 170.50); account 3 is the last group and keeps 147.00.",
